course: dictionary
lesson: 11009
title: Watercolour: a paint and a picture
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can name two different things. Watercolour is one of them. It can name the paint itself: «Watercolour is thin paint mixed with water.» The clues are thin and mixed with water, so this is the paint.
explain: It can also name a picture made with that paint. «Picture Hannah's watercolour sky bleeding into the sea.» A sky is something you paint, not something you pour, so here a watercolour means a painting.
explain: Use the clues around the word to decide which meaning fits. Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Watercolour is a kind of paint that you mix with water.
fact: Watercolour gives light, see-through colours.
fact: «A watercolour» means a picture painted with watercolour paint.
fact: «Watercolour» can be an adjective too, as in «a watercolour painting».
fact: Wet paper makes watercolour spread, and waiting for it to dry stops the colours bleeding.
exercise: «Watercolour can sometimes be lifted with a tissue, and spills can be turned into clouds.» What does watercolour mean here? | *A kind of paint mixed with water | A wooden brush | A tissue | A glass of clean water
exercise: «Picture Hannah's watercolour sky bleeding into the sea.» Here, a watercolour means | *A painting made with watercolour paint | A kind of cloud | A bottle of water | A stormy sea
exercise: «Different paints behave differently: watercolour is thin and spreads in wet paper, acrylic is plastic-based.» Which paint spreads in wet paper? | Chalk | *Watercolour | Acrylic | Pencil
test: «Rinse watercolour and acrylic brushes in water.» What is watercolour in this sentence? | A brush | *A kind of paint | A bucket | A type of tissue
test: Hannah hangs her watercolour in the hall. What is her watercolour? | *A picture painted with watercolour paint | A bowl of water | A tin of cleaner | A wet sponge
exam: «Oil paint dries slowly so painters can blend it smoothly for days.» Watercolour is different from oil paint because | It dries slowly, so it can be blended for days | It is made of plastic | *It is thin and spreads on wet paper | It must be cleaned with a special cleaner
